## Github Action Rules

- Check if `pubspec.yaml` exists in project root and summarize key scripts
- Check if `.env.example` exists in project root to identify key `env:` variables
- Always use `env:` variables and secrets attached to jobs instead of global workflows
- Extract common steps into composite actions in separate files

2) (Ask if needed) Use <tool>"Run Terminal"</tool> to check package info on pub.dev and verify it's not deprecated:

```bash
dart pub info {package_name}
```

3) (Ask if needed) Use <tool>"Run Terminal"</tool> to fetch package README and check for deprecation notices:

```bash
curl -s https://pub.dev/packages/{package_name} | grep -i "discontinued\|deprecated\|archived" || echo "Package appears active"
```

4) (Ask if needed) In case of package issues, check the pubspec.yaml directly from the source repository:

```bash
curl -s https://raw.githubusercontent.com/{owner}/{repo}/refs/heads/{main/master}/pubspec.yaml
```